ither time did that go anywhere  what is it what's different this time  either in terms of the political  environment you're introducing it in or  in terms of your strategy of how to  actually get it passed no I don't think  it's going to get passed with a  Republican Republicans control the house  of the Senate I've never suggested that  but i think it is becoming more and more  apparent  the American people that something is  fundamentally wrong in this country when  so few have so much and so many have so  little so senator as you know we did a  poll because para Paul's one and I will  win in New Hampshire to try to get a  sense of how voters are thinking about  you you've got a quarter of the vote  about in both Iowa and New Hampshire up  from our previous polls in those states  and dependents are being pretty  supportive of you this morning on  Morning Joe I asked senator McCaskill  your colleague about you and your  chances I want you to listen to what she  said I think the media is giving Bernie  a pass right now I very rarely read in  any coverage of Bernie that he's a  socialist I think he would like to see  Medicare for all in this country he  would like to see expansion of  entitlement he would like to see he does  not worried about a debt at all he is  somebody who I think is frankly against  trade he's against a whole lot of things  yeah are unrealistic in this day and age  so senator I know you'd like to stay  away from personality and talk about  issues so let me ask you on the issues  senator McCaskill raised and suggested  they were part of your socialist beliefs  and made you unelectable guilty as  charged or you wanna you want to clarify  the record it's I find it surprising  that she says that the media doesn't  refer to me as a socialist is no article  that I've seen that doesn't refer to me  as a Democratic Socialist I am do I  believe in a medicare-for-all  single-payer system absolutely do I  believe in opposition to Senator  McCaskill that we need trade policies  that are fair to the American worker and  not just benefit CEOs of large  corporations I plead guilty I think we  need to change our trade policies we  couldn't think of another instance in  which one of your Democratic Senate  colleagues has spoken out against you  that way have you heard people speak out  against you that way and why do you  think senator McCaskill is now I to the  best of my knowledge this is the first  time that a colleague has attacked me  you'll have to ask senator McCaskill why  I think it's unfortunate I as you know  and I know I bore you guys sometimes the  death but I am trying to run  issue oriented campaign and not one of  personal attacks just to be clear  senator Sanders you never bore us you're  always a hundred percent delightful I  want to ask you a little bit more about  this poll and again we'll try to keep  we're in a state stick with issues but  just think about the you you've gained  ground in both Iowa and New Hampshire  and our poll and others on Hillary  Clinton we dug a little deeper though  and looked at some at some of the  underlying data and it's there's some  places where you're clearly behind her  one of them is with women where she  dominates you fifty nine percent to 19  and I was 64 to 19 in New Hampshire I'm  going to ask you to make the case to  female voters as to why you they should  support you day in particular should  support you over Hillary Clinton  especially given that she would be a  historic figure for that gender in and I  do understand that and you're absolutely  right there are millions of women who  are excited about the possibility of a  woman for the first time becoming  president of the United States I fully  understand that appreciate that I think  on the other hand if you look at my  economic agenda that says two women  workers you can't keep working for ten  or twelve dollars an hour we need to  raise the minimum wage to fifteen  dollars an hour we are going to unveil a